selfhost-dashboard: visual theme for BookStack (spec 0002, Faz 1)
==================================================================

What this folder is
  A BookStack visual theme (APP_THEME=selfhost-dashboard). It overrides two views and adds three
  partials. It runs as server-side code inside BookStack, so every file here is reviewed like code.

Files (UPSTREAM lists every one of them in ALLOW)
  home/default.blade.php     exact copy of the pinned upstream view + one @include('selfhost.home') line
  shelves/show.blade.php     exact copy of the pinned upstream view + one @include('selfhost.shelf') line
  selfhost/home.blade.php    dashboard block (guests see nothing), includes selfhost.cards
  selfhost/cards.blade.php   BookStack, Penpot and Plane cards
  selfhost/shelf.blade.php   project header and latest books for shelves tagged plane-project
  UPSTREAM                   pin: BOOKSTACK_IMAGE, VIEW_ROOT, sha256 of each original view, ALLOW list
  PHP_ALLOWLIST              functions the partials may call
  ACCESS_ALLOWLIST           object/method access the partials may perform (exact chains)
  README                     this file
  There is no functions.php and no public/ directory, and there must never be one (CB-7 d).

Shelf tag (lower case, exactly)
  Add a tag named  plane-project  to a shelf, value = the project code (letters and digits, 1-12).
  The first such tag in id order decides. A tag named Plane-Project is not a candidate.

Rules that cannot be relaxed (spec 0002 section 6.1)
  1. The override views are byte-identical to upstream except added lines of the exact form
     @include('selfhost.<name>') (tests/cb8_upstream_check.py).
  2. Partials pass the two-stage scan (tests/blade_scan): Blade source, then Blade-compiled output.
  3. Any change to PHP_ALLOWLIST or ACCESS_ALLOWLIST needs a full appsec review.
  4. A BookStack bump changes only the BookStack line in stacks/bookstack/versions.env and the
     BOOKSTACK_IMAGE line here (tests/upgrade_diff_check.sh); anything else is a full review.
  5. If the pinned image changes and the views differ, delete ALL overrides and their VIEW/ALLOW
     lines together (all or nothing), then port again in a separate PR.
